a goal and an assist, Shane Pinto and Stephen Halliday scored and the Ottawa Senators defeated the New Jersey Devils 4-1 on Monday night to keep their hot start going.","story":"NEWARK, N.J. -- — Tim Stützle had a goal and an assist, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565255/shane-pinto\">Shane Pinto</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5136706/stephen-halliday\">Stephen Halliday</a> scored and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ott/ottawa-senators\">Ottawa Senators</a> defeated the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a> 4-1 on Monday night to keep their hot start going.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3069285/linus-ullmark\">Linus Ullmark</a> stopped 29 of the 30 shots he faced, allowing just a goal to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4915855/arseny-gritsyuk\">Arseny Gritsyuk</a> with five minutes left. After a tumultuous summer that included <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/brady-tkachuk-florida-panthers-eef8ef1a3b87088c8eccc06https://apnews.com/article/brady-tkachuk-florida-panthers-eef8ef1a3b87088c8eccc06978d08587978d08587\">trading captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4319858/brady-tkachuk\">Brady Tkachuk</a></a> to Florida, the Senators have won five of their first six games, despite missing a handful of key players to injuries.\n\n\r\n              Their depth took another hit when defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5174232/nikolas-matinpalo\">Nikolas Matinpalo</a> was injured in the first period. Matinpalo went head first into the boards when he was boarded by New Jersey’s <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042037/anthony-mantha\">Anthony Mantha</a>.\n\n\r\n              Matinpalo received medical attention and did not return, ruled out with what the team called an upper-body injury.\n\n\r\n              Ottawa was already thin on the blue line with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697386/jake-sanderson\">Jake Sanderson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4712021/artem-zub\">Artem Zub</a> sidelined. And forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874721/william-eklund\">William Eklund</a> is out for what coach Travis Green estimated to be <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/senators-william-eklund-93aa04604b2301553162b918684741fb\">an extended period of time</a> because of an injured left ankle.\n\n\r\n              Green's team has made up for those absences with timely scoring and fast-paced play. The breakthrough at the Devils came 9 seconds into the second period when Pinto scored his first goal of the season, beating <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697683/nico-daws\">Nico Daws</a> (16 saves) off the rush following a pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3149829/michael-amadio\">Michael Amadio</a>.\n\n\r\n              Halliday scored on the power play midway through the second when he was left open in front by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3025535/brett-pesce\">Brett Pesce</a> losing his footing. That was the Senators finally taking advantage of the Devils parading to the penalty box after failing to score on Mantha’s 5-minute major earlier.\n\n\r\n              Fans booed as the clock ran out before the second intermission, on the way to the home team falling to 2-3-0 while struggling to incorporate a handful of new faces into the lineup.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Senators: Host St. Louis on Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              Devils: Visit Detroit on Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-13T01:46:30Z"}}